"Acts 21:3–6":[43,[[21,3,"After sighting Cyprus and passing south of it, we sailed on to Syria and landed at Tyre, where the ship was to unload its cargo."],[21,4,"We sought out the disciples in Tyre and stayed with them seven days. Through the Spirit they kept telling Paul not to go up to Jerusalem."],[21,5,"But when our time there had ended, we set out on our journey. All the disciples, with their wives and children, accompanied us out of the city and knelt down on the beach to pray with us."],[21,6,"And after we had said our farewells, we went aboard the ship, and they returned home."]]],
