"1 Timothy 3:14–15":[53,[[3,14,"Although I hope to come to you soon, I am writing you these things"],[3,15,"in case I am delayed, so that you will know how each one must conduct himself in God’s household, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth."]]],
"1 Timothy 3:15":[53,[[3,15,"in case I am delayed, so that you will know how each one must conduct himself in God’s household, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth."]]],
"1 Timothy 4:13":[53,[[4,13,"Until I come, devote yourself to the public reading of Scripture, to exhortation, and to teaching."]]],
"1 Timothy 4:14":[53,[[4,14,"Do not neglect the gift that is in you, which was given you through the prophecy spoken over you at the laying on of the hands of the elders."]]],
"1 Timothy 5:3":[53,[[5,3,"Honor the widows who are truly widows."]]],
"1 Timothy 5:16":[53,[[5,16,"If any believing woman has dependent widows, she must assist them and not allow the church to be burdened, so that it can help the widows who are truly in need."]]],
"1 Timothy 5:17":[53,[[5,17,"Elders who lead effectively are worthy of double honor, especially those who work hard at preaching and teaching."]]],
"1 Timothy 5:17–19":[53,[[5,17,"Elders who lead effectively are worthy of double honor, especially those who work hard at preaching and teaching."],[5,18,"For the Scripture says, “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain,” and, “The worker is worthy of his wages.”"],[5,19,"Do not entertain an accusation against an elder, except on the testimony of two or three witnesses."]]],
"1 Timothy 5:20":[53,[[5,20,"But those who persist in sin should be rebuked in front of everyone, so that the others will stand in fear of sin."]]],
"1 Timothy 5:22":[53,[[5,22,"Do not be too quick in the laying on of hands and thereby share in the sins of others. Keep yourself pure."]]],
"2 Timothy 1:6":[54,[[1,6,"For this reason I remind you to fan into flame the gift of God, which is in you through the laying on of my hands."]]],
"2 Timothy 1:13–14":[54,[[1,13,"Hold on to the pattern of sound teaching you have heard from me, with the faith and love that are in Christ Jesus."],[1,14,"Guard the treasure entrusted to you, with the help of the Holy Spirit who dwells in us."]]],
"2 Timothy 2:1–2":[54,[[2,1,"You therefore, my child, be strong in the grace that is in Christ Jesus."],[2,2,"And the things that you have heard me say among many witnesses, entrust these to faithful men who will be qualified to teach others as well."]]],
"2 Timothy 2:2":[54,[[2,2,"And the things that you have heard me say among many witnesses, entrust these to faithful men who will be qualified to teach others as well."]]],
"2 Timothy 3:10–11":[54,[[3,10,"You, however, have observed my teaching, my conduct, my purpose, my faith, my patience, my love, my perseverance,"],[3,11,"my persecutions, and the sufferings that came upon me in Antioch, Iconium, and Lystra. What persecutions I endured! Yet the Lord rescued me from all of them."]]],
"2 Timothy 3:14":[54,[[3,14,"But as for you, continue in the things you have learned and firmly believed, since you know from whom you have learned them."]]],
"2 Timothy 3:16–17":[54,[[3,16,"All Scripture is God-breathed and is useful for instruction, for conviction, for correction, and for training in righteousness,"],[3,17,"so that the man of God may be complete, fully equipped for every good work."]]],
"2 Timothy 4:1–2":[54,[[4,1,"I charge you in the presence of God and of Christ Jesus, who will judge the living and the dead, and in view of His appearing and His kingdom:"],[4,2,"Preach the word; be prepared in season and out of season; reprove, rebuke, and encourage with every form of patient instruction."]]],
"2 Timothy 4:2":[54,[[4,2,"Preach the word; be prepared in season and out of season; reprove, rebuke, and encourage with every form of patient instruction."]]],
"2 Timothy 4:5–7":[54,[[4,5,"But you, be sober in all things, endure hardship, do the work of an evangelist, fulfill your ministry."],[4,6,"For I am already being poured out like a drink offering, and the time of my departure is at hand."],[4,7,"I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, I have kept the faith."]]],
"2 Timothy 4:6–7":[54,[[4,6,"For I am already being poured out like a drink offering, and the time of my departure is at hand."],[4,7,"I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, I have kept the faith."]]],
